{"name":"Yellow Pepper","hex":"#eeef06","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"yellow pepper","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any type of pepper or chili pepper having a yellow flesh and skin when ripe."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow_pepper"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bell pepper","blocks":[{"text":"The bell pepper is the fruit of plants in the Grossum Group of the species Capsicum annuum. Cultivars of the plant produce fruits in different colors, including red, yellow, orange, green, white, and purple. Bell peppers are sometimes grouped with less pungent chili varieties as \"sweet peppers\". While they are botanically fruits—classified as berries—they are commonly used as a vegetable ingredient or side dish. Other varieties of the genus Capsicum are categorized as chili peppers when they are cultivated for their pungency, including some varieties of Capsicum annuum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Green-Yellow-Red-Pepper-2009.jpg/330px-Green-Yellow-Red-Pepper-2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bell_pepper","wikidata":"Q1548030"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow","wikidata":"Q943"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Colorful_Bell_Peppers.JPG/500px-Colorful_Bell_Peppers.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Colorful_Bell_Peppers.JPG/1280px-Colorful_Bell_Peppers.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Colorful_Bell_Peppers.JPG/500px-Colorful_Bell_Peppers.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A variety of colored bell peppers","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AColorful_Bell_Peppers.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/November_15%2C_2012%2C_The_Right_Cut_%288223639251%29.jpg/500px-November_15%2C_2012%2C_The_Right_Cut_%288223639251%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/November_15%2C_2012%2C_The_Right_Cut_%288223639251%29.jpg/500px-November_15%2C_2012%2C_The_Right_Cut_%288223639251%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chef chopping bell peppers","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANovember_15%2C_2012%2C_The_Right_Cut_(8223639251).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Aspen-PopulusTremuloides-2001-09-27.jpg/500px-Aspen-PopulusTremuloides-2001-09-27.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Aspen-PopulusTremuloides-2001-09-27.jpg/1280px-Aspen-PopulusTremuloides-2001-09-27.jpg?utm_sourc